# portdata/ is runtime data, not source. Git must hand a clone exactly the bytes
# that were committed: tools/deploy_portdata.py compares file CONTENTS to decide
# what to copy into assets/ and both bin/ trees, so a line-ending conversion on
# checkout would make raid1.lvl differ between a Windows and a Linux clone and
# report itself stale forever. (The parser itself takes CRLF or LF - see
# RaidLevel.cpp - so this is about reproducibility, not about it loading.)
portdata/** -text
